## selfhost::lower — AST → x86_64 GAS back end.
##
## The lowering pass: it walks the expression AST **post-order** and emits real x86_64
## GAS assembly for a stack machine (operands pushed, then the operator pops two and
## pushes the result) into a `StrBuf`. Proven end-to-end by `tests/selfhost_codegen_e2e`
## — the emitted `.s` is assembled, linked, and run, and its exit code is the computed
## value (`2 + 3 * 4 - 1` → 13) — promoted here, the arithmetic core of the GAS back end.
##
## This module now also emits **whole function definitions** with locals (item 6's
## function-storage shape): a `Decl` of kind 1 (`name := fn(p0, p1) -> R { <stmts> <ret> }`)
## lowers to a labelled callee with a frame prologue/epilogue, the parameters spilled from
## their argument registers (`%rdi`/`%rsi`) to frame slots, the body statement list (local
## `Assign` bindings + `While` loops) lowered, and the trailing return expression delivered
## in `%rax`. A `Var` reads its frame slot; the name→slot map is a `Vec(SlotEntry)` keyed by
## the variable's source name **span** (content-compared via `str_at`, mirroring nameres's
## env). The per-shape runtime is proven by `selfhost_var_codegen_e2e` (frame + slot
## load/store), `selfhost_loop_codegen_e2e` (counted loop / back-edge), and
## `selfhost_call_codegen_e2e` (callee label, %rdi arg, %rax result, `ret`); lower.al itself
## is type-check-only via `selfhost_tree_e2e`.
##
## The operator bytes match the rest of the tree (the lexer/parser token kinds):
## 16 `+`, 17 `-`, 18 `*`, 19 `/`, 29 `%`; and the comparisons 20 `==`, 24 `<`, 25 `>`,
## 26 `<=`, 27 `>=`, 28 `!=` (each materialized as a 0/1 boolean on the stack via
## `cmpq` + `setcc` + `movzbq`). Control flow — `if`/`else` and `match` — lowers over
## **fresh labels** threaded through an `in out` counter (so nested branches never
## collide), mirroring the proven branch machinery in `selfhost_branch_codegen_e2e` /
## `selfhost_mini_compiler_e2e`. The AST types are shared from `selfhost::ast` (sibling
## submodule) via local comptime aliases (Modules §4.1) — the emitter lowers the SAME
## `Expr`/`Decl`/`Stmt` the parser produced, no redeclaration. A `Var` lowers to a
## frame-slot read (the slot resolved by name span).
## The GAS output buffer is now `rt::StrBuf` (off `alloc::strbuf` for the §1 fixpoint). Aliasing
## the `rt` module as `strbuf` keeps every `strbuf::StrBuf` type + `push_str`/`push_int` call
## resolving to rt's analogues unchanged — no per-site churn.
strbuf := rt
vec := alloc::vec
(Arg, Arm, Bind, Decl, Expr, FieldDecl, Param, Stmt, local_type_span, local_is_uninit, local_is_mut) := ast
(bnd_ns, bnd_nl, bnd_next) := ast
fld_p := ast::fld_p
param_p := ast::param_p
arm_p := ast::arm_p
arg_p := ast::arg_p
stmt_p := ast::stmt_p
