    ## top), then popped into the argument registers in REVERSE order (the last-pushed pops
    ## first) — argument `i` → register `argreg(i)` (%rdi %rsi %rdx %rcx %r8 %r9). The callee
    ## is invoked by its source name as the label; its result (%rax) is pushed back onto the
    ## stack like any other expression value. `nargs` is the argument count; `args_head` the
    ## arena-linked `Arg` list head.
    Expr::Call(cs, cl, nargs, args_head) => {
