      ## the callee NAME is read for anything: the name span this node carries is BORROWED from the callee
      ## chain's root variable (see `ast::ecallee_mark`), so every name-keyed path below — the builtins,
      ## the fn-value SLOT path (`fs` genuinely has a slot: the array's base), the direct call — would
      ## resolve it to the wrong thing. The parser's site set is the only arbiter.
      if ecallee_is(cs) {
