      ## `compiles(...)` must never reach ordinary call lowering. The sema pass rewrites these
      ## nodes when it runs, but build lowering can receive a fresh AST; fold with the same
      ## bounded, side-effect-free predicate used by `comptime if` and leave a bool word on the
      ## value stack. A malformed arity is fail-closed rather than emitted as an undefined call.
      if callee == "resolves" or callee == "compiles" {
        if nargs == 1 {
          qa := arg_expr_at(args_head, 0, a)
