## Per-fn Var→VReg map (names are params + body locals; a fresh id per distinct name). Temps take
## further fresh ids (not recorded here). All ids MUST stay < 32 (the allocator's vreg capacity) — the
## predicate's conservative estimate keeps admitted fns well under, and a leaked over-cap vreg fails loud
## in `ra_verify_no_vreg` (never a silent miscompile).
mut IRV_S : [usize; 64] = [0; 64]
mut IRV_L : [usize; 64] = [0; 64]
mut IRV_V : [usize; 64] = [0; 64]
mut IRV_N := 0        ## recorded named vregs
mut IRV_NEXT := 0     ## next fresh vreg id (named + temps)
mut IRL_N := 0        ## next fresh IR-internal label id (< 16)

## COMMIT 5 — per-fn CALL side-table. A `call` IR inst (op 6) carries a Sym operand whose value is an
## INDEX into this table (a name span can't fit an i64). Each entry records the callee-name span + the
## enclosing module (for bare-call resolution), replayed at render time through `emit_mangled_call` — the
## SAME mangler the text path uses, so the emitted symbol is byte-identical to the callee's own def label.
mut IRC_CS : [usize; 32] = [0; 32]   ## callee-name span start
mut IRC_CL : [usize; 32] = [0; 32]   ## callee-name span length
mut IRC_MS : [usize; 32] = [0; 32]   ## enclosing module span start (caller's module)
mut IRC_ML : [usize; 32] = [0; 32]   ## enclosing module span length
mut IRC_N := 0                        ## recorded calls (< 32)
## An argument-lowering STACK: each `ir_lower_call` lowers its args to operands (nested calls resolve
## fully + pop before an outer call records its own args), then moves them into the SysV arg registers.
## A stack (not a flat per-call array) so a nested call `f(a, g(b), c)` never clobbers the outer call's
## already-lowered `a` while lowering `g`'s `b`.
mut IRCA_K : [usize; 32] = [0; 32]
mut IRCA_V : [i64; 32]   = [0; 32]
mut IRCA_TOP := 0

## COMMIT 6 — per-fn BARRIER side-table. A construct the scalar-leaf IR does NOT model (this commit: a
## SCALAR field read `p.f` of a by-ref struct param) is emitted through the EXISTING TEXT emitter
## (`emit_gas`) at render time, bracketed by a FULL-CLOBBER IR inst (op 14) so every live scalar vreg
## spills across it. Each barriered value expr's `ptr(Expr)` is recorded here (a raw pointer can't fit an
## i64 operand); at render the barrier replays `emit_gas` (which reads the struct param from its TEXT frame
