## the following `mov <vreg>, %rax` copies it into the result vreg.
mut IRBR_E : [usize; 16] = [0; 16]
mut IRBR_N := 0

## COMMIT 6d — per-fn STATEMENT-BARRIER side-table. A STATEMENT the scalar-leaf IR does NOT model (this
## commit: an inline SCALAR array local's array-literal INIT `ys := [10,20,3,9]`) is emitted through the
## EXISTING text emitter (`emit_array_assign`) at render, bracketed by a FULL-CLOBBER IR inst (op 23) so
## every live-across scalar vreg spills. Unlike the value barrier (op 14) it yields NO %rax result — the
## text emit just writes the array's element words into their FRAME slots. Each entry records the
## ArrayLit value expr's `ptr(Expr)` (a raw pointer can't fit an i64 operand) and the array's BASE slot.
